 - For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
 - A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the caller as a rejection, and also runs `onError` with the thrown error and then `afterSession`, because the call sits inside the same `try`/`finally` as the rest of the turn. An `afterSession` hook called under this condition can infer the session never advanced past `beforeSession`: no user-input hooks ran, no model response was generated, and no tool rounds were started — a cleanup hook that allocates in `beforeSession` and frees in `afterSession` will therefore always see the allocation and the release on the same error path ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession when it throws, and still rejects to the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
 
+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and what it receives as `usage` is the turn's total, specified below rather than recorded.
+
+- The `usage` it receives sums every provider call of the turn, so a turn that ran tools is counted whole and a deployer billing or budgeting from the hook is not handed only the last leg ([validated by: reports the sum of every round that reported, not the last round alone](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+- A round whose provider reported no usage contributes nothing to that total rather than ending it: the rounds that did report are still summed ([validated by: keeps counting the rounds that reported when a round in between reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L89)).
+- A turn whose rounds report no usage at all still reports no usage ([validated by: still reports nothing when no round in the turn reported usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L102)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it has always reported — the one provider call's usage — so the common path does not move ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
